CORE
main.c
--unwind 4 --rounds 3 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
Value counterpart of `thread_local_through_pointer`: each thread increments
its own copy of `static __thread unsigned slot = 7` through `&slot` and
checks it is 8. With the initialisation recorded in the spawning thread
after the spawn, it could take effect after the increment, and the check
failed.

Reported FAILED before the fix, SUCCESSFUL after. See
`thread_local_through_pointer_value_real`, which must stay FAILED.
